From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: XGKICK reset leaves the 64 KB packet buffer alone

What it is for:
  resetScheduler (run at every VU program start, VU1 and VU0
  microprograms alike) and startXgkick (every XGKICK) reset the XGKICK
  state with `m_xgkick = {}`, which also zeroes its 64 KB packet buffer.
  A sampling profile of the Ben 10 port's game thread on Windows (MSVC
  Release, first level) put about 11% of the thread in that memset.

The change:
  - XgkickPipeline::resetControl() sets every field but the buffer back
    to its initial value; resetScheduler and startXgkick use it.
  - Exact: the buffer is only read below copiedBytes (the GIF tag at a
    qword just copied, and the packet up to totalBytes when the last tag's
    end has been copied), and every one of those bytes is copied in from
    VU memory first.
  Same results. Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; the Ben 10 port's 40 captured
  VU1 workloads give the same checksums and cycle count with and without
  its translated code.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vu1.h
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_vu1.h
@@ -248,6 +248,23 @@
         uint64_t issueCycle = 0;
         bool active = false;
         bool currentTagEop = false;
+
+        // Everything but the packet buffer back to its initial value. The
+        // buffer is only read below copiedBytes, and those bytes are always
+        // copied in first, so it needs no clearing: zeroing its 64 KB at
+        // every program start and every XGKICK cost about a tenth of the
+        // game thread on Windows (findings/21 s.8).
+        void resetControl()
+        {
+            sourceAddress = 0;
+            totalBytes = 0;
+            copiedBytes = 0;
+            currentTagEnd = 0;
+            cycleCredit = 0;
+            issueCycle = 0;
+            active = false;
+            currentTagEop = false;
+        }
     };
 
     static constexpr uint32_t kFmacLatency = 4u;
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_core.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_core.cpp
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
     m_vfWritePipeline = {};
     m_viWritePipeline = {};
     m_accWritePipeline = {};
-    m_xgkick = {};
+    m_xgkick.resetControl();
     m_vfReady = {};
     m_viReady = {};
     m_accReady = {};
@@ -630,7 +630,7 @@
         return;
 
     const uint32_t sourceAddress = (qwordAddress * 16u) % m_activeVuDataSize;
-    m_xgkick = {};
+    m_xgkick.resetControl();
     m_xgkick.active = true;
     m_xgkick.sourceAddress = sourceAddress;
     m_xgkick.cycleCredit = 1u; // XGKICK's issue cycle counts toward PATH1.
